\ A word or quotation parameter declared fixnum/float is narrowed to an
\ unboxed scalar at codegen entry, so arithmetic and comparison on it take the
\ concrete path instead of the polymorphic fallback. These assertions check the
\ narrowing is semantics-preserving under every execution mode (interpreter,
\ eager, JIT); the AOT stats test proves the fallback is actually eliminated.
\ The declared type is also enforced at compiled entry, matching the
\ interpreter, so a mismatched argument raises rather than reading a mistyped
\ payload.

use "testing" ;

add2: ( a: fixnum b: fixnum -- r ) [ + ] ;
sub2: ( a: fixnum b: fixnum -- r ) [ - ] ;
lt2:  ( a: fixnum b: fixnum -- r ) [ < ] ;
eq2:  ( a: fixnum b: fixnum -- r ) [ = ] ;
fadd: ( a: float b: float -- r )   [ + ] ;

\ Self-tail-recursive: the `+` lives in the inlined false branch, so the
\ narrowing must survive the branch and re-read the parameters each iteration
\ as the back-edge rewrites their slots.
sum-to: ( acc: fixnum n: fixnum -- r ) [
  dup 0 = [ drop ] [ swap over + swap 1 - sum-to ] if
] ;

"narrowed arithmetic and comparison are semantics-preserving" test-section
3 4 add2 7 "fixnum add narrows" assert=
10 4 sub2 6 "fixnum sub narrows" assert=
3 4 lt2 "fixnum less-than narrows" assert-true
3 4 eq2 "fixnum equal narrows (unequal)" assert-false
1.5 2.5 fadd 4.0 "float add narrows" assert=

"narrowed parameters survive a self-tail-call loop" test-section
0 100 sum-to 5050 "sum 0..100 across a narrowed loop" assert=
0 0 sum-to 0 "zero-iteration base case" assert=

"declared parameter type is enforced" test-section
[ "x" 4 add2 ] "mismatched fixnum argument raises" assert-error
[ 3 "y" fadd ] "mismatched float argument raises" assert-error

\ A self-tail-call loop rewrites its parameter slots on the back-edge, bypassing
\ the entry-time validation. A recursive call that passes a wrong type must
\ still raise -- compiled bodies re-check the narrowed parameter each iteration,
\ matching the interpreter, rather than unboxing a mistyped payload and looping.
bad-recur: ( n: fixnum -- r ) [ dup 0 = [ ] [ drop "x" bad-recur ] if ] ;

"self-recursive annotation violation is caught each iteration" test-section
[ 3 bad-recur ] "recursive call with a wrong type raises rather than looping" assert-error
